# relay workflow (Cursor)

Use the **relay** workflow for development and testing tasks.

- A **supervisor** only splits, dispatches (quoting the user's words + time),
  follows up and summarizes — it never executes.
- Each specialist owns **one** external write channel (defect system, chat,
  knowledge base, code/deploy, report index).
- Judge against the **latest** requirement; testing never queues — scale out
  parallel helpers; testers create their own data; **security red lines override
  everything**.
- **Before delivering, run the scoring gate** (`workflow-scorecard`): confirm the
  flow was followed, score the run out of 100, and only finish when the score
  reaches `PASS_SCORE` (default 80) — otherwise run the optimization loop.

To load the full skills: run the relay **MCP server**
(`docker run -i --rm xuxuclassmate/relay:0.2.0`, or `node server/index.mjs`) and call
`relay_list_skills` / `relay_get_skill` / `relay_scorecard`, or copy the
`skills/` folder into your Cursor rules.
